course: dictionary
lesson: 14458
title: Pare: cut it back
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To pare something is to cut away its thin outer skin or edge, usually with a small knife. «Mum will pare the apple before we eat it.» The skin comes off, and the apple is ready to eat.
explain: Pare can also mean to make something smaller bit by bit. «We need to pare down the list of guests» means we must cut it to the most important names. Look at the clues around the word: a knife, skin or edge means cutting off, and words like down or back mean making less.
explain: Pare is a verb, so it changes its form: pares, pared, paring. «Dad pared the potatoes yesterday.» «He is paring his nails now.» To check which meaning fits, ask whether the sentence is about skin or edges, or about making something smaller.
fact: Pare means to cut away the thin outer skin or edge of something.
fact: Pare is often used for fruit, such as apples, and for things like nails.
fact: A paring knife is the small knife you use to pare fruit.
fact: «Pare down» means to cut something down to its most important parts.
fact: «Pare back» means to reduce something bit by bit, such as spending.
exercise: «Sam pared the apple with a small knife.» What does pared mean here? | Dropped it on the floor | *Cut away the thin skin | Painted it bright red | Ate it whole
exercise: The council wants to pare down the list of projects. What does pare down mean? | Put the list in a box | Ask everyone to vote for every project | *Cut down to the most important ones | Add lots more projects
exercise: Find the word in «Dad pared the potatoes» that is the past tense of pare. | *pared | Dad | potatoes | the
test: «Jo wants to pare back her spending each week.» What does pare back mean? | Count her money in a bank | Give money to her friends | Spend much more money | *Reduce spending bit by bit
test: Which tool would you use to pare an apple? | A spoon for soup | A hammer | A paintbrush | *A small paring knife
exam: «The chef pared the thin skin from the lemon, then pared down the recipe to four ingredients.» In «pared down the recipe», what does pared down mean? | Put it in a box | *Cut it down to the important parts | Added many more ingredients | Made it longer
